## Gaussian prescribed split

Primary: Swee Hong Chan, Gil Kalai, Bhargav Narayanan, Natalya Ter-Saakov, Moshe White, *Unimodality for Radon partitions of random vectors*, arXiv2507.01353v1 (2July2025), DCG published7September2026, DOI10.1007/s00454-026-00870-6, Conjecture7.2(2).

For every d>=1,n>=d+2, take n independent standard Gaussian vectors in R^d and set q_k=P(conv(X_1,...,X_k) meets conv(X_(k+1),...,X_n)), with empty group probability0. The target is q_k^2>=q_(k-1)q_(k+1) for all interior k. This concerns a fixed prescribed split; it is not the size distribution of a randomly chosen unique Radon part when n>d+2. No parameter instance is nominated.

Read actual source Theorem1.3 proof and Lemma5.1 proof and concluding question; compare actual published Section7.2. The one-dimensional kernel at n=d+2 gives a random sign vector. At n>d+2, one needs existence of a sign-constrained vector in a higher-dimensional random kernel. Taking a union over vectors does not preserve the association inequality used in the proof. That is an unproved step, not a source refutation.

Actual original r47 discovery and its concluding objection reopened: White2507.05449 already supplies the Crofton parity sum and d1 formula. The simple sufficient intrinsic-volume-row log-concavity is false; r47 exhibits n6,r2. A valley in one intrinsic-volume row is not a valley in the entire parity sum. No new checks repeat those observations. r116 explicitly rejected this same target as old.

The preprint and author PDF display a wrong relation between p_k and q_k in Section7; the journal displays p_k=binom(n,k)q_k/2, as exchangeability requires. We use the published event definition and scope and do not nominate this correction.

Strongest falsifier of any claimed full proof: an unclosed existential-event transfer from rank1 to higher random kernels. A genuine counterexample must rigorously bound the full q probabilities for an actual n,d,k and show q_k^2<q_(k-1)q_(k+1). None supplied. EXCLUDED AS OLD, not declared solved.

